Dillo host packaging for Ubuntu Resolute
=======================================

The packaging/ubuntu-resolute branch is the source for the Launchpad
recipe targeting ppa:nmccallum/pichi, resolute only. It is also pushed as
bot/dillo/packaging-ubuntu-resolute at the same tip. It contains debian/,
the crates pinned by Cargo.lock in vendor/, and Cargo's complete
.cargo/config.toml, including the Arma, Burrow, Devtree and PMI Git source
redirects. LICENSE.dependencies records the bundled crates' licenses and
notices and is installed in /usr/share/doc/dillo-vm/.

This branch uses source format 3.0 (native), with version 0.1.0 matching
the upstream Cargo version. All sources are in one tree. Launchpad does
not need a separate orig tarball or a networked prepare-source step.
Build the recipe from packaging/ubuntu-resolute, with no source preparation
command. The previous quilt proposal is superseded by this branch.

After installing Build-Depends, source and binary builds need no network
or warm Cargo cache. From a checkout of this branch, run:

    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc
    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

For a clean Resolute build with a locally configured sbuild chroot:

    sbuild --dist=resolute ../dillo-vm_0.1.0.dsc

debian/rules gives Cargo a private home and always builds with:

    cargo build --offline --locked --release -p dillo --bin dillo

It uses /usr/bin/cargo and /usr/bin/rustc from Build-Depends, rather than
rustup's pinned nightly toolchain. Rust >= 1.91 is required by smoltcp.
RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 permits Cargo to parse the test-only artifact dependencies
with [unstable] bindeps. SMOLTCP_IFACE_MAX_ADDR_COUNT=4 preserves Dillo's
IPv4 and IPv6 gateway and DNS addresses.

The clean target preserves vendor/, including Cargo.toml.orig files
covered by Cargo's checksums. debian/source/options replaces dpkg-source's
default exclusions so vendored files such as .gitmodules also survive
source packaging. It installs the native host binary to
/usr/bin/dillo. Source and binary package names are dillo-vm; Conflicts:
dillo prevents co-installation with the unrelated Dillo browser. Builds
are intended for native amd64 and arm64 builders. The package test runs
only dillo --help; VM tests need KVM and cross-built firmware and guest
binaries and remain outside the package build.

To refresh dependencies, use a networked machine with the upstream pinned
nightly toolchain and Python >= 3.11. Update Cargo.lock deliberately, then
run from the repository root:

    cargo --config net.offline=false vendor --locked --versioned-dirs vendor

Replace the [source] tables in .cargo/config.toml with the generated source
configuration, including all Git source redirects. Retain the existing
[unstable], [target], and [env] settings and one [net] section with
offline = true. Then regenerate the bundled notices:

    python3 debian/update-vendor-licenses

Commit vendor/, Cargo.lock, the configuration and notices together.
Review upstream changes before updating this packaging branch. Archive
setup is handled separately; this branch does not upload to Launchpad.
